WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.620
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.300
Today I will show you some papers&nbsp;
and results with Stable Diffusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:16.980
a free and open source image generator AI. And&nbsp;
I cannot believe how good these results are.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:24.600
First, we had an earlier example with ControlNet&nbsp;
and dancing. This means that in goes something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:30.360
for instance, a video of us, and out&nbsp;
comes a hand drawn anime version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.960
it. Now, the advantage of this is&nbsp;
that we don’t need to look perfect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:40.560
and we don’t even need to be at this exact&nbsp;
place in the background, because all of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:48.060
can be synthesized. And today, someone took&nbsp;
this idea to the next level. Look. And now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:55.380
if you think this is a blue haired woman converted&nbsp;
into to a more painterly blue haired woman… well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:02.820
have a look at this. Oh yes, we don’t even need&nbsp;
to be the character we want to be, we just need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:13.620
to kind of look like the character we want to&nbsp;
be. This is going to be an amazing tool for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:20.160
digital artists of the future. And remember,&nbsp;
this needs a tiny bit of time and expertise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:26.220
but it is something that you can run for&nbsp;
free on your own machine, and some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:31.440
other examples, even in your pocket, on&nbsp;
your smartphone. What a time to be alive!

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:37.980
Two, we can even use Stable Diffusion’s&nbsp;
ControlNet to provide it input images for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:44.760
it to redraw. For instance, we can give it this&nbsp;
childhood drawing, and we can ask this little AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:51.300
to create a super high quality version of&nbsp;
it. My goodness. This is incredibly good.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:58.140
Three, now here is a crazy idea. Why not give&nbsp;
it a QR-code as an input image, and see what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:04.140
happens? Well, these look great…so this was&nbsp;
a good thought experiment, but of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:11.580
these won’t work as QR codes. Just as a piece&nbsp;
of art. Wait a second. Hold on to your papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:18.120
Fellow Scholars, do they actually work as QR-codes&nbsp;
and are they readable from a smartphone camera?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:24.000
Yes they are! Make sure to play with the distance&nbsp;
a bit, perhaps increase the distance a little,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:32.880
but every single one of these work for me. I&nbsp;
can’t believe it. Artificial creativity. Wow.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:38.880
Four, and these video to video workflows&nbsp;
are becoming so incredibly good that…are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.180
you seeing what I am seeing? Can that&nbsp;
really be? These can now be generated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:51.420
almost immediately. If we wish to create a&nbsp;
smoother video, we would have to wait a bit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:58.800
but not in the order of hours. Just in the&nbsp;
order of seconds, and super quick previews&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:05.820
can be done like this. This would not have been&nbsp;
possible just a few months ago. Unbelievable.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:11.580
Five, with the right prompts, Stable&nbsp;
Diffusion can also create an 1800s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:18.720
version of our favorite rockstars. Elton John,&nbsp;
Freddie Mercury, Dave Grohl, Hendrix or Jagger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:25.320
you name it. I love how creative some of&nbsp;
these solutions are and how they retain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:30.960
their looks and personalities while&nbsp;
putting them into an 1800s setting.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:35.220
Six, we can also create custom portraits for our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.760
dungeons and dragons characters.&nbsp;
Just give the AI the description,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:44.040
and there we go. The prompts and the workflow&nbsp;
for some of these images are available,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:50.880
which means that you can likely reproduce&nbsp;
and tweak them yourself at home. So good.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:58.500
Seven, in the meantime, Google just published&nbsp;
a really cool paper on how to guide these image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:05.340
generator AIs with natural language. First,&nbsp;
we can ask for an image of a giant macaron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:13.320
and croissant in front of the Eiffel Tower. Well,&nbsp;
yes, I hear you saying, Doc, with today’s papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:20.400
that is not surprising. What is surprising&nbsp;
is that without generating a new image,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:26.160
we can swap these objects, enlarge&nbsp;
the macaron, and if we don’t like it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:33.840
replace it with a different one, or even better&nbsp;
use our own photo and ask it to recapture its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:39.660
appearance. Which it had done really well as&nbsp;
the lighting now also has an effect on these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:45.240
objects as well. Not just the background&nbsp;
is different, everything is different. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:51.420
interacting with text to image AIs via&nbsp;
natural language. How cool is that?

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:58.200
Eight, creating zoom videos has also improved&nbsp;
a great deal. Now we can choose a few images,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.920
and stitch them together to&nbsp;
create these zoom videos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.780
and they are now really smooth. Previous&nbsp;
ones had some flickering issues,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:14.820
but this one is now so much better. And all this&nbsp;
improvement in just a few months! Unbelievable.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:18.300
I put a link to all of these&nbsp;
works in the video description,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.420
and for now, let the experiments begin!

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:24.420
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

